      "body": "## Summary\n- `remove_all` used `list.remove` for a one-item set, so only the first match was deleted.\n- A request object queued twice could stay in `running` after it was supposed to be removed.\n- The single-item path now drops every equal element in place. The multi-item path still returns a new list.\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] `pytest tests/v1/core/test_sched_remove_all.py` (not run here: this machine has no torch, so importing the scheduler pulls in torch)\n",
